            <chunk name="Object" index="169">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">92191b7b-2e95-4a8d-a5f5-5d2d7b883cd8</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">version</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Heath → Honeybee + Foton
Version 0.2.0 — 2026-11-09

Rebuilds a Heath request with stock Honeybee/Foton components as ONE model for daylight and energy. The Heath backend uses a detailed daylight room and a simpler energy model, so results differ a little: energy here includes the detailed windows and shades, daylight includes the other floors around the room.

How to use:
1. Paste the Heath JSON into the request panel.
2. Check the sliders.
3. Run steps 1–3 in order (the red groups).

Requires Rhino 8, Ladybug Tools 1.8+, Foton 0.3.6 (Package Manager), OpenStudio 3.9.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
